(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #108 aliasing probe: `append orig to items` stores
 orig's pointer as a list element - the list now names the same string.
 `orig` must not be freed on its own later `Set`, or the list's element
 would dangle. A buffer append (byte-consuming) is the different case a
 sibling test in this pair (piece/sink in the cargo unit tests) checks.)

a number called n is 5.
a text called orig is "{n}".
a list called items is [].
append orig to items.
Set orig to "changed".
Print element 1 of items.
